<Information title="Privacy Policy" description="How Nikola Pešić handles website visits, email enquiries and free prelaunch call bookings for CLOSEFLOW AI.">
 <p>This notice covers the CLOSEFLOW AI marketing website, enquiries and prelaunch calls. It does not describe a functioning AI product: the agent has not been built, and the website does not connect to social accounts or process real client DMs.</p>
 <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
 <p><strong>Nikola Pešić</strong>, an individual based in <strong>Serbia</strong>, operates the project and is responsible for personal information received through enquiries and bookings. CLOSEFLOW AI is a project name, not a registered company. Contact the operator at <a href="mailto:nikolapesic878@gmail.com">nikolapesic878@gmail.com</a> for privacy questions or requests.</p>
 <h2>2. Information and purposes</h2>
 <ul>
  <li><strong>Website visits:</strong> GitHub Pages hosts this website. GitHub processes technical request information, which may include IP addresses, browser/device information and access logs, for hosting, security and service operation.</li>
  <li><strong>Scripted preview:</strong> all names, messages and lead details are fictional. Selecting a stage does not submit information, create a lead record or save your activity in browser storage.</li>
  <li><strong>Call bookings:</strong> Calendly collects the information you provide, such as your name, email address, chosen time/time zone and any optional booking answers or guests you add. The operator uses booking details to arrange, manage and follow up on the conversation. Calendar invitations and confirmations also contain scheduling information.</li>
  <li><strong>Email enquiries:</strong> the operator receives your address, message and information you choose to send through Gmail, to answer your enquiry and help with scheduling.</li>
  <li><strong>Calls:</strong> Zoom processes participant names, connection/device information and live meeting audio/video needed to provide the call. The operator does not record calls or use automated transcription or AI meeting summaries for these prelaunch conversations. Brief business follow-up notes may be included in the email conversation.</li>
 </ul>
 <p>There is no newsletter signup, automated marketing list or separate CRM for this prelaunch workflow. Booking a call does not subscribe you to promotional messages. The website code includes no advertising pixels, analytics SDKs, embedded Calendly widget or third-party chat widget. Please do not share passwords, private client conversations or health information.</p>
 <h2>3. Legal bases</h2>
 <p>Where applicable law requires a legal basis, responding to voluntary business enquiries, arranging meetings and keeping limited follow-up records are based on the operator’s legitimate interests in communicating with interested coaches and developing the concept. Where an enquiry concerns a potential contract, steps taken at your request may also be a basis. Necessary legal records are kept to meet legal obligations. If any future processing relies on consent, you can withdraw it without affecting prior lawful processing.</p>
 <p>Providing enquiry or booking information is voluntary. Without the information needed to contact you, the operator may be unable to respond or arrange a call. No automated decision-making or profiling with legal or similarly significant effects is carried out by this website.</p>
 <h2>4. Service providers and international processing</h2>
 <p>GitHub provides hosting, Calendly provides scheduling, Google/Gmail provides email communications and related invitations, and Zoom provides conferencing. These providers process information to deliver their services and may process some technical/account information for their own purposes. The operator receives enquiries and booking details and does not sell them or pass them to advertisers.</p>
 <p>Provider systems may process information outside Serbia, the UK or the European Economic Area, including in the United States. Their processing and available transfer arrangements are described in their notices and applicable service terms; this website does not promise that data stays in a particular country.</p>
 <ul><li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub Privacy Statement</a></li><li><a href="https://calendly.com/legal/privacy-notice">Calendly Privacy Notice</a> and <a href="https://calendly.com/legal/data-processing-addendum">Data Processing Addendum</a></li><li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a></li><li><a href="https://www.zoom.com/en/trust/privacy/privacy-statement/">Zoom Privacy Statement</a></li></ul>
 <h2>5. Cookies and browser storage</h2>
 <p>The website’s own code does not set cookies or use local/session storage. It does not embed or preload the booking service. Following a Calendly or other external link takes you to that provider, where its own cookies, controls and privacy practices apply. GitHub’s technical hosting processing is separate from the scripted preview.</p>
 <h2>6. Retention and security</h2>
 <p>The operator’s retention policy is to review and delete enquiry messages, booking/calendar records and business follow-up notes under the operator’s control no later than six months after the last related enquiry or call. This is a manual operating process, not an automatic deletion feature of the website. Records may be kept longer where required by law or necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal claims, limited to that purpose.</p>
 <p>Providers may retain their own security logs or backup copies under their policies. Deletion from the operator’s active records does not imply immediate removal from every provider backup. Access to operator-held enquiries is limited to running the prelaunch project; no online service can guarantee absolute security.</p>
 <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
 <p>Depending on applicable law, you may request access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability or object to processing. Some rights are subject to legal exceptions. Send requests to <a href="mailto:nikolapesic878@gmail.com">nikolapesic878@gmail.com</a>. The operator may ask for proportionate identity verification and will respond within the period required by applicable law.</p>
 <p>You can complain to the competent data-protection authority, including Serbia’s Commissioner for Information of Public Importance and Personal Data Protection, the UK Information Commissioner’s Office or the relevant EEA authority, where applicable. Nothing here limits mandatory privacy rights.</p>
 <h2>8. Audience and future changes</h2>
 <p>This site is intended for adult professional coaches. It does not invite children’s information or clients’ health data. Contact the operator if such information has been sent by mistake.</p>
 <p>New AI functionality, account integrations, marketing or analytics would require a review of these practices and an updated notice before being introduced. Material changes will be reflected here with a revised effective date. For project information, visit <a href={pageUrl('contact/')}>Contact</a>.</p>
</Information>
